\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Jesus calls us! O'er the tumult
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Of our life's wild restless sea,
\par Day by day his voice is sounding,
\par Saying, 'Christian, follow me'.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.   As, of old, Saint Andrew heard it
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj By the Galilean lake,
\par Turned from home and toil and kindred,
\par Leaving all for his dear sake.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Jesus call us from the worship
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Of the vain world's golden store,
\par From each idol that would keep us,
\par Saying, 'Christian, love me more'.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. In our joys and in our sorrows,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Days of toil and hours of ease,
\par Still he calls, in cares and pleasures,
\par 'Christian, love me more than these'.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  Jesus calls us! By your mercy,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Saviour, make us hear your call,
\par Give our hearts to your obedience,
\par \pard      Serve and love you best of all.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

